[H1] FR12-02 - Climate control of a stock of textiles
[P1] A small municipal museum keeps costumes, flags and fragments of cloth in a reserve that had not been renovated for several years when new shelves were installed. The curator took advantage of the relocation of the collections to verify the climatic conditions of the room. Three independent recorders were placed at different heights, away from windows and direct air outlets. They measured the temperature and relative humidity every ten minutes for six weeks. Measures and reorganisation
